# Files exempt from the 700-line limit. Keep this list small and
# documented — every entry is a deliberate decision the team agreed on.
#
# Format: one path per line (relative to repo root). Lines starting
# with `#` are comments. Lines ending with a reason after `# —` are
# preferred so future maintainers can re-evaluate exceptions.

src/notebook/drawing/engine/stroke.js  # — Ported from upstream demo. Documented "deltas" track edits relative to upstream file boundaries; splitting would break the diff-check workflow described in README-DRAWING.md.

src/notebook/state.ts  # — Pointer-interaction state machine (~lines 465–960) is tightly coupled to shapes/selectedIds/camera/undo. Extraction was evaluated and judged to add a conceptual seam without proportional gain. Revisit if the state machine grows further.

src/notebook/renderer.ts  # — Single cohesive canvas draw pipeline (background → grid → shapes → selection chrome). Splitting would scatter z-order ordering across files for no real gain; sits beside state.ts which is excepted for the same reason.

src/notebook/notes-canvas.ts  # — Canvas controller + render-state assembly + gesture wiring, tightly coupled to state.ts and renderer.ts. Extraction adds a seam without proportional gain; revisit if it grows materially.

src-tauri/src/settings.rs  # — A single `#[derive(Deserialize)]` Settings struct (one field per persisted setting) plus its Default impl. serde derive needs every field in one struct, so the registry can't be split across files. Keep additions tight.
